  "narrative": "Final scientific report for the supplied lung-lineage CRISPR dataset after the H6 validation response. H6 assessment: SMARCA4 loss versus stronger dependency_SMARCA2 is accepted and closed; discovery signed effect +0.784 (95% CI +0.765 to +0.803) and independent validation signed effect +0.790 (multiplicity-corrected interval +0.760 to +0.820 at alpha 0.00385) are concordant. Because the hypothesis direction is -1, positive signed effects correspond to raw SMARCA4-loss minus SMARCA4-intact mean differences about -0.78 to -0.79, i.e. much more negative dependency_SMARCA2 and therefore stronger SMARCA2 dependency in SMARCA4-deficient lines. The magnitude is far above the 10% relative clinical benchmark and is precise enough to support a dataset-level synthetic-lethal-like association, not causality or external generalizability. Supported findings: the central accepted map is SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H6, now independently validated); MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency (H8, validated); TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency (H49, validated); CDKN2A loss -> stronger MDM2 dependency (H59, validated); PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency (H103, validated); KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H17 discovery accepted, supported by context validation H24 and many robust contexts). Context evidence: PTEN-STAT3 is amplified in high IFN-gamma signature (H156) and remains large in both high and low IFN-gamma strata (H160, H161); it is also accepted in high EMT, high stemness, and high aneuploidy contexts. SMARCA4-SMARCA2, WRN-MSI, KEAP1-NFE2L2, CDKN2A-MDM2, and TP53-USP7 effects are robust across library, screen-quality, Cas9-quality, mutation-burden, aneuploidy, growth-rate, lineage-subtype confirmations where tested, including newly accepted adenocarcinoma confirmations H188 and H192. Negative findings: same-gene driver dependency contrasts are largely unsupported or null, including BRAF V600E for BRAF dependency (H1), EGFR amplification for EGFR dependency (H3, rejected after validation), ERBB2 amplification for ERBB2 dependency (H4 near-null), and KRAS mutation for KRAS dependency (H2 small and inconclusive). MYC amplification is not a useful broad dependency modifier in the tested outcomes and does not modify TP53-USP7 or CDKN2A-MDM2 effects in the available interaction tests. RB1-loss versus DHX9 failed independent validation (H84/H90) and should not be considered replicated. MTAP co-deletion as a clinically meaningful MDM2 modifier is not supported: the narrow CDKN2A-loss/TP53-wild-type claim failed independent validation (H162) and remaining MTAP tests are underpowered or imprecise. Specificity probes against non-matched outcomes are mostly near null, supporting pathway/locus specificity rather than broad screen artifacts, though some probes are not tight enough to prove absence. Unresolved uncertainty: some near-null intervals for KRAS, ERBB2, PTEN-WRN, and MTAP context remain imprecise; direct global independent validation for KEAP1-NFE2L2 (H17) was not separately requested, although context validation and replication across eligibility strata are strong; several active context/lineage/AXL tests are unestimated. Most informative next analysis: use remaining analysis slots for the already registered active follow-ups rather than new broad scans, prioritizing AXL-expression context interactions for PTEN-STAT3, KEAP1-NFE2L2, and MSI-WRN (H196-H198), lineage-subtype main effects for WRN-MSI, SMARCA4-SMARCA2, TP53-USP7, and PTEN-STAT3 (H187, H189, H190, H191), and biological context modifiers with meaningful interval boundaries (H168, H171, H174, H183, H184, H185, H151, H176); if capacity remains, the residual high-screen-quality MTAP check (H178) can be used as a last specificity probe. No further voluntary validation requests remain, and all conclusions should be read as associations in this supplied dataset, not causal mechanisms or generalized claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 13 final synthesis. H6 SMARCA4-SMARCA2 independently validated and closed. Core accepted validated map: SMARCA4-SMARCA2, MSI-WRN, TP53-USP7 weaker, CDKN2A-MDM2, PTEN-STAT3; KEAP1-NFE2L2 weaker is discovery-accepted and context-validated. MTAP closed/not supported after H162 validation reversal. Negative same-gene driver and MYC modifier effects; RB1-DHX9 not replicated. Next allocate analyze slots to active AXL context H196-H198, adenocarcinoma confirmations H187/H189/H190/H191, and key contexts H168/H171/H174/H183/H184/H185/H151/H176; H178 residual MTAP only if capacity. No validation requests remain; associations only."
}
